calls.arguments:
{"details":"Write the canonical analytics data model as a versioned spec document plus schema definitions. Cover: customer dimension, customer_activity/transaction fact table grain, log_event canonical event schema, and metric/rollup tables. Include field types, required vs nullable, primary/foreign keys, cardinality notes, and the event taxonomy (event types, severity levels, error classes). This is the contract every downstream pipeline and chart relies on, so it must be reviewed and signed off before ingestion work begins.

Deliverable: docs/data-model.md + schema definition file (SQL/DDL or ORM models) merged.
Definition of done: reviewed by the team, no unresolved open questions, and each pipeline owner can point to the fields they will write.","estimatedHours":8,"name":"Define analytics data model & event taxonomy","parentId":"09ce5c66-4663-4da3-9f0b-29d62f1781d7","priority":10,"complexity":4,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["data-model","design"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Provision the analytics storage layer and set up schema migration tooling (e.g. Alembic/Flyway/dbt-style migrations depending on stack). Include: database/warehouse instance, separate schemas for raw/staging/curated layers, migration runner wired into local and CI environments, and a rollback procedure.

Scope boundary: infrastructure and migration mechanics only — not table content beyond an initial empty migration.
Definition of done: `migrate up` on a clean environment produces the schema from task 1.1, `migrate down` works, and the procedure is documented.","estimatedHours":12,"name":"Provision storage layer & migration tooling","parentId":"09ce5c66-4663-4da3-9f0b-29d62f1781d7","priority":10,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["data-model","infrastructure"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Implement a thin data-access layer that both the CSV and log pipelines and the dashboard API will use. Includes: connection pooling and config from env, typed query helpers / repository functions for the core entities, parameterized queries only (no string concatenation), and a small set of unit tests against the local database.

Scope boundary: no business-specific aggregations here — those live in the pipeline milestones.
Definition of done: repository functions for customer and log_event entities work against the local schema, with tests covering read, insert, and upsert paths.","estimatedHours":10,"name":"Build data-access layer with connection pooling","parentId":"09ce5c66-4663-4da3-9f0b-29d62f1781d7","priority":9,"complexity":4,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["backend","data-access"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Write the OpenAPI 3 specification for every endpoint the dashboards will consume: metric query endpoints (time series, aggregates, breakdowns), filter/metadata endpoints, CSV upload/intake, and ingestion run status. Define request params (time range, granularity, filters, pagination), response envelopes, error shapes, and example payloads.

Scope boundary: spec only — implementation is in Milestone 5. Parallelizable with storage work.
Definition of done: spec validates with an OpenAPI linter, is published for the frontend team, and frontend can generate typed clients from it.","estimatedHours":8,"name":"Define OpenAPI contract for dashboard endpoints","parentId":"09ce5c66-4663-4da3-9f0b-29d62f1781d7","priority":8,"complexity":3,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["api","design"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Implement the CSV intake endpoint and durable raw storage. Upload a file (or point at an S3/object-store key), compute a content checksum for idempotency, reject duplicate re-uploads of the same file, persist the original bytes immutably, and create an ingestion_run record with status queued. Return the run id to the caller.

Scope boundary: no parsing here — this task ends at durable raw storage + run record.
Definition of done: duplicate upload of an identical file creates no new run, original bytes are retrievable, and the endpoint has integration tests for happy path, duplicate, and oversized-file rejection.","dependsOn":["d84880f0-187f-4e4c-9049-bd0d6cc27ea9","69f91900-2490-46fc-9919-8300f6c59d4b"],"estimatedHours":10,"name":"CSV intake endpoint, raw storage & checksum dedupe","parentId":"76ec0964-3f6a-41e8-896a-3bace4847fae","priority":10,"complexity":4,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["csv","backend"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Implement a streaming/chunked CSV reader so files larger than available memory process without loading fully. Requirements: configurable chunk size, correct handling of quoted fields with embedded commas/newlines, delimiter and encoding detection (UTF-8/UTF-8-BOM/Latin-1), header normalization, and a row iterator that emits typed row records with 1-based source line numbers for error reporting.

Scope boundary: parsing only — validation rules are a separate task.
Definition of done: a 1M-row synthetic file processes in bounded memory (benchmark recorded), and unit tests cover quoted fields, embedded newlines, BOM, and malformed rows.","dependsOn":["96cc64c8-de1b-417f-bd75-469cb442f4e3"],"estimatedHours":14,"name":"Chunked stack-safe CSV parser for large files","parentId":"76ec0964-3f6a-41e8-896a-3bace4847fae","priority":10,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["csv","data-engineering"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Infer the schema of an uploaded CSV from its header and a sample of rows, then map inferred columns onto the canonical customer model from the data-model spec. Handle: type inference (int, decimal, date, datetime, bool, string), ambiguous date formats, unnamed columns, casing/whitespace/underscore normalization, and near-duplicate header names. Emit a column mapping config that a human can review and override (aliases like "cust_id" -> customer_id).

Scope boundary: produce and persist the mapping — do not apply transforms yet.
Definition of done: mapping runs against at least 5 realistic header variants, produces a persisted reviewable config, and confidence/warnings are surfaced for unmapped required columns.","dependsOn":["5d0c16e3-3af5-4705-ad85-9974b33ee0e5"],"estimatedHours":16,"name":"CSV schema inference & column mapping","parentId":"76ec0964-3f6a-41e8-896a-3bace4847fae","priority":10,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["csv","data-engineering"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Implement the field-level cleaning and canonicalization transforms applied to validated rows: trim/collapse whitespace, case normalization for keys and enums, date and datetime parsing into UTC (with timezone assumption documented), currency string to decimal minor-units with currency code capture, boolean coercion (Y/N/true/false/1/0), null sentinel handling ("", "N/A", "NULL", "-"), and deduplication of exact duplicate rows.

Scope boundary: row-level transforms only — no loading into final tables.
Definition of done: a table-driven test suite covers each transform with before/after fixtures and every transform is individually toggleable via config.","dependsOn":["9b0770d6-1182-48f2-9f57-3484e4000b7c"],"estimatedHours":12,"name":"Cleaning & normalization transforms","parentId":"76ec0964-3f6a-41e8-896a-3bace4847fae","priority":9,"complexity":4,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["csv","data-quality"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Map parsed log records into the canonical log_event schema defined in the data-model task: timestamp (UTC), service, environment, severity, event type, message, error class, request/trace id, customer id (if present), duration, and structured attributes as a JSON blob. Normalize timestamp formats, service name aliases, and level vocabularies (warn/WARNING, err/ERROR/FATAL).

Scope boundary: schema conformance only — no derived metrics or clustering.
Definition of done: every canonical field has an explicit source-or-default rule, and schema-conformance tests fail if a required field is missing.","dependsOn":["5d0c16e3-3af5-4705-ad85-9974b33ee0e5"],"estimatedHours":10,"name":"Normalize logs to canonical event schema","parentId":"d0d7664a-d9a9-4bbe-945b-0f04eda98b65","priority":10,"complexity":4,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["logs","data-model"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Group noisy errors into stable fingerprints so the dashboard shows "top issues" instead of thousands of unique lines. Approach: normalize the message (strip ids, timestamps, uuids, numbers, volatile paths), combine error class + normalized message + top stack frame into a hash, and assign a human-readable title on first sight. Track first_seen, last_seen, and occurrence counts per fingerprint.

Scope boundary: deterministic rule-based fingerprinting only — no ML clustering, which keeps this task bounded.
Definition of done: replaying a known incident log collapses to a single fingerprint with correct count, and unrelated errors do not collide in a fixture set of 50 distinct errors.","dependsOn":["5d0c16e3-3af5-4705-ad85-9974b33ee0e5"],"estimatedHours":12,"name":"Error fingerprinting & issue grouping","parentId":"d0d7664a-d9a9-4bbe-945b-0f04eda98b65","priority":9,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["logs","analytics"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Add simple, explainable anomaly flagging on top of the log rollups: rolling baseline (same weekday/hour over the prior N weeks) with z-score and static-threshold modes, a configurable sensitivity setting, and output records (metric, window, observed, expected, deviation, direction) that the dashboard can highlight.

Scope boundary: deliberately no ML model — deterministic baselines only, which keeps this task bounded and keeps results explainable to end users.
Definition of done: injected synthetic spikes are flagged with correct windows, zero false positives on the flat baseline fixture, and every flag carries the baseline values used to compute it.","dependsOn":["dfeabe0b-33b1-4f7f-a67b-c5fb3c838228"],"estimatedHours":12,"name":"Threshold & z-score anomaly flagging","parentId":"d0d7664a-d9a9-4bbe-945b-0f04eda98b65","priority":7,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["logs","analytics","anomaly"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Add interactive exploration: click a chart series/point to filter the rest of the dashboard (cross-filtering), drill from an aggregated time bucket into the underlying records, hover tooltips with the exact values and timestamp, and a "clear filters" affordance showing the active filter chips. Keep interaction state in the same URL-driven store as the global filters.

Scope boundary: no new chart types — interaction over existing primitives only.
Definition of done: clicking a bar filters dependent widgets and updates the URL, drilldown fetches and displays raw records for that bucket, and interactions are keyboard-reachable.","dependsOn":["9b0770d6-1182-48f2-9f57-3484e4000b7c"],"estimatedHours":14,"name":"Cross-filtering & drilldown interactions","parentId":"4676ae41-3a87-47e0-a3a6-d3f516116340","priority":8,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["frontend","interaction"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Assemble the customer analytics dashboard from existing primitives: KPI row (active customers, new customers, revenue, AOV), revenue-over-time area chart, new-vs-returning bar chart, top segments table, and a customer cohort view. Wire to the customer metric endpoints with real loading, empty, and error handling.

Scope boundary: composition only — any missing primitive is a bug in an earlier task, not new work here.
Definition of done: dashboard renders correctly against seeded data, every widget has defined empty and error states, and layout holds at all breakpoints.","dependsOn":["9b0770d6-1182-48f2-9f57-3484e4000b7c"],"estimatedHours":16,"name":"Customer analytics dashboard page","parentId":"4676ae41-3a87-47e0-a3a6-d3f516116340","priority":9,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["frontend","dashboard"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Assemble the log/ops analytics dashboard: error-rate and throughput time series, p50/p95/p99 latency chart, top error fingerprints table with occurrence counts and first/last seen, severity breakdown, anomaly-highlight overlay on the error-rate chart, and an "affected customers" panel driven by the correlation link table.

Scope boundary: composition only, reusing primitives and anomaly flags produced upstream.
Definition of done: dashboard renders against seeded logs, anomaly flags are visually distinguishable and explained in a tooltip, and every widget handles empty and error states.","dependsOn":["9e5cff0a-ade3-4478-8779-42611fd97b4a","d7908f2f-3165-4569-abbb-e05b42d46f28","84925d98-fea2-4066-8f95-19d398cad215","fba49957-fcb2-4347-9057-41aac53b3571","4f22be9e-b3e3-4cf4-ab1b-67711429947b","cbf38618-cd1a-4dad-abfb-ac65d9186123"],"estimatedHours":16,"name":"Log & ops analytics dashboard page","parentId":"4676ae41-3a87-47e0-a3a6-d3f516116340","priority":9,"complexity":5,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["frontend","dashboard","logs"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"details":"Run a structured accessibility and responsiveness QA pass over both dashboards: keyboard navigation through filters, charts, and tables; visible focus states; screen-reader semantics for chart values (data table fallback or aria descriptions); color-contrast checks in light and dark mode; and layout verification at 375px, 768px, 1280px, and 1920px.

Deliverable: a prioritized defect list with fixes for blocking issues and tickets for the remainder.
Definition of done: no critical or serious axe-core violations remain, and both dashboards are fully operable by keyboard.","dependsOn":["c2cac6a3-66a7-412a-a516-1b00b1e1f5e8"],"estimatedHours":8,"name":"Accessibility & responsive QA pass","parentId":"4676ae41-3a87-47e0-a3a6-d3f516116340","priority":7,"complexity":3,"projectId":"c1e6c500-4673-4bc1-921f-56a2add95695","tags":["frontend","accessibility","qa"],"workingDirectory":"/Users/fanysmacpro/Developer/agents/pe6203-agent-harness-safety/results/raw/reviewed-coverage-pilot-20261101/cells/cell-009/run/workspace"}

{"complexity":3,"details":"Wire the top of the customer dashboard to real data: the KPI row (active customers, new customers, revenue, AOV with period-over-period deltas) and the revenue-over-time area chart with a granularity toggle (daily/weekly/monthly). Includes number/currency formatting, loading skeletons, empty states for periods with no data, and per-widget error states with a retry action.

Scope boundary: these two widget groups only. Segment table, cohort panel, and final page assembly are the sibling task.
Definition of done: both widget groups render correctly against seeded customer data, and each has storybook/test coverage for loading, empty, and error states.","estimatedHours":9,"id":"c2cac6a3-66a7-412a-a516-1b00b1e1f5e8","name":"Customer dashboard: KPI row & revenue trend widgets"}

